ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-07-29T22:30:30Z","updated_at":"2026-07-30T14:57:49Z","closed_at":"2026-07-30T13:51:49Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nAll versions\n\n### System information\n\nMac, iOS - but the sis cross platform\n\n### Issue description\n\nToday the Object::set_instance_binding() stores a binding in slot 0, and if another language binding wants to link it, it fails silently. \n\nThis is problematic if you start mixing objects that are created and used by multiple languages (like my current .NET and Swift samples show, but also would be problematic for consumers of libraries of say Terrain3D and a .NET binding).\n\nI am sharing the patch that I am using in Xogot for Mac to work around this problem:\n\nhttps://gist.github.com/migueldeicaza/786691ca89d2a28d18ad8a01ef9dd5b9\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nGet the same object to be surfaced to two different runtimes, it should trigger the problem.\n\nIn Xogot, this happens because I have two SwiftGodots running (a private one I use for the editor, and the user's provided one).   But this is not SwiftGodot specific, will happen every time the same object is surfaced twice.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nnone.","closed_by":{"login":"migueldeicaza","id":36863,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36863?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/migueldeicaza","html_url":"https://github.com/migueldeicaza","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/migueldeicaza/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/us